    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Dodgy Album is the debut studio album by British rock band Dodgy, released in 1993 on A&M Records. Produced by Ian Broudie, it introduced the group’s buoyant, melody-driven style, blending Britpop-era guitar pop with an indie-rock edge and a light, upbeat feel that drew attention from the British music press.\n\nThe album includes some of Dodgy’s early signature songs, including “Water Under the Bridge” and “Lovebirds,” and it helped establish the band on the early-1990s Camden scene. Though it was not a major chart breakthrough, the record laid the groundwork for the wider success Dodgy would achieve later in the decade, and it remains a key document of their early sound.",
